.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt POLICYCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm policyctl
.Nd create and inspect software attribute policy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Ar program
.Op Ar attribute ...
.Nm
.Cm validate | explain
.Ar bundle.cap
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
uses the bundle parser and verifier used by SwitchBoard.
.Cm init
prints an exec-only Unit.ucl for a program basename and zero or more attributes.
It validates all arguments before emitting output.
Place this policy beside the unit's
.Pa bin/program
and declare the unit in the bundle's Bundle.ucl.
.Cm validate
parses and verifies the complete bundle.
.Cm explain
performs the same checks and prints JSON containing each unit's label,
exec activation flag, attributes, and published endpoints with their
requirements.
.Pp
These commands operate on files, without contacting SwitchBoard or resolving
UNIX users or groups.
They do not install policy or grant authority.
Validation does not prove that executable contents are signed, that runtime
admission will succeed, or that a bundle has been activated.
Use
.Xr switchboardctl 8
for static cross-bundle coverage and authorized runtime reloads.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Invalid policy or invalid policy arguments return 2.
Invalid command usage returns 64.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libcapbundle 3 ,
.Xr switchboardctl 8
